From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Windows' names for This PC and the Recycle Bin

The shell's own names are Wine's: "My Computer" and "Trash", and the confirmation that deleting a file asks is worded for a Trash. Windows 11
calls them "This PC" and "Recycle Bin" and asks "Are you sure you want to move ... to the Recycle Bin?". English strings only.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc b/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc
--- a/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc
@@ -148,8 +148,8 @@
 
         /* special folders */
 	IDS_DESKTOP		"#msgctxt#display name#Desktop"
-	IDS_MYCOMPUTER		"My Computer"
-	IDS_RECYCLEBIN_FOLDER_NAME      "Trash"
+	IDS_MYCOMPUTER		"This PC"
+	IDS_RECYCLEBIN_FOLDER_NAME      "Recycle Bin"
 	IDS_CONTROLPANEL	"Control Panel"
 
         /* context menus */
@@ -172,10 +172,10 @@
 	IDS_DELETEITEM_TEXT "Are you sure you want to delete '%1'?"
 	IDS_DELETEMULTIPLE_TEXT "Are you sure you want to delete these %1 items?"
 	IDS_DELETESELECTED_TEXT "Are you sure you want to delete the selected item(s)?"
-	IDS_TRASHITEM_TEXT "Are you sure that you want to send '%1' to the Trash?"
-	IDS_TRASHFOLDER_TEXT "Are you sure that you want to send '%1' and all its content to the Trash?"
-	IDS_TRASHMULTIPLE_TEXT "Are you sure that you want to send these %1 items to the Trash?"
-	IDS_CANTTRASH_TEXT "The item '%1' can't be sent to Trash. Do you want to delete it instead?"
+	IDS_TRASHITEM_TEXT "Are you sure you want to move '%1' to the Recycle Bin?"
+	IDS_TRASHFOLDER_TEXT "Are you sure you want to move the folder '%1' and all its contents to the Recycle Bin?"
+	IDS_TRASHMULTIPLE_TEXT "Are you sure you want to move these %1 items to the Recycle Bin?"
+	IDS_CANTTRASH_TEXT "The item '%1' can't be moved to the Recycle Bin. Do you want to delete it permanently instead?"
 	IDS_OVERWRITEFILE_TEXT "This folder already contains a file called '%1'.\n\nDo you want to replace it?"
 	IDS_OVERWRITEFILE_CAPTION "Confirm file overwrite"
 	IDS_OVERWRITEFOLDER_TEXT "This folder already contains a folder named '%1'.\n\
